The integration of these components reveals significant gaps between the desired outcomes and existing financial infrastructure. The requirement for indefinite appreciation without speculation or utility removes the standard drivers of market value. While the smart contract can record ownership and display a rising nominal number, the translation of that number into purchasing power relies on market participants accepting the valuation without fundamental reasons to do so.

